# The old-channel thread and the injury rescue. Arc, owners and plants:
# content/STORY_BIBLE.md (spoilers). Voice: content/STYLE.md.
# Thread owners (`who ow_*`) are cast once per voyage and never overlap.

card m_carrier
type event
cat mystery
clue core
due
once
days 15 19
roles A
when !is A ow_list
when !is A ow_song
when !is A ow_garden
when !is A ow_letter
when !is A ow_dose
text {A}'s arrival-test dish scans the old common channel toward Mars; no one on Earth has listened there since the relay was written off. A week of integration shows a faint carrier. Folded at 10.96 seconds, 2.4 percent duty, it stands up like a fence post. "An alias," {A} says. "Something of ours."
do who ow_hail A
do mark t_carrier

card m_alias
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 19 20
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when since t_carrier >= 4
when fired m_theory
text {A} asks {B} to point a second dish at the carrier. Anything aboard would alias differently per ship. The bursts land on both in the same millisecond and slide against fleet time by about two seconds a day: the fleet's closing rate on Mars. "Not aboard, then," {A} says, and books the dish again.
do bond A B 3
do open dec_signal

card dec_signal
type decision
cat mystery
days 19 20
weight 1
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean curious open log
when fired m_alias
when is A ow_hail
text If it's the grey relay, it may still know a standard hello. {A} wants the ground's clearance to answer every burst with one, signed with the old program key the fleet still carries as a relay fallback: a courtesy, and a test. {B} points out that every reply ties up the comms computer.
option open | Answer every burst | The ground clears it inside a day: hello only, nothing that commands. {A} adds one line to the comms schedule, and the first hello goes out at 14:02, timed to the millisecond. {B} files one line of dissent, signed, and leaves it there.
  set signal_answered
  mark t_signal
  morale B -3
  trait A curious 5
option log | File it, keep going | The carrier goes into the anomaly file under "later". {A} clips the folded trace inside the binder, just in case, and the comms computer stays on the letters. {A} writes a dissent, signed; {B} countersigns it.
  set signal_ignored
  mark t_signal
  morale A -5

card signal_reply
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 25 26
roles A
when flag signal_answered
when is A ow_hail
do mark t_frame
text Stacked over a week of bursts, the receiver pulls out half a frame of housekeeping on the old channel, in a format the receiver has to look up, cut off partway. The fleet's answers go out on schedule, every one. {A} forwards the scrap home, and Mission Control replies six minutes later: "say again."
do trait A curious 4

card signal_echo
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 25 27
roles A
when flag signal_ignored
when is A ow_hail
do mark t_frame
text Folding a week of noise, {A} finds half a frame of housekeeping on the old channel, in a format the receiver has to look up, cut off partway. Averaged over a day, its period hasn't moved by a millisecond. The anomaly report calls it "persistent".
do morale A -3

# Injury and rescue: needs supplies from another ship.
card c_hail
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 39 39
roles A
when is A ow_hail
text {A} works out how many times the old-channel carrier has knocked since the fleet first heard it: close to half a million. Every gap has a reason, Mars in the way or a cold night, and every knock lands on the beat. "Half a million. Every gap explained. Out," {A} sends.
do trait A curious 1

card crisis_eva
type event
cat grim
once
days 10 34
weight 6
roles A
when cond A ok
when kit_elsewhere A
text During {A}'s scheduled EVA a tether snags on a bracket and wrenches {A}'s arm, with the next ship closed up and a suited crewmate clipped in at its hatch. {A} frees it, secures every tool, works back along the line hand over hand, and comes inside with a wrist that won't bend.
do cond A injured
do who eva_who A
do morale A -10
do open rescue_kit

card rescue_kit
type rescue
cat grim
duration 1
roles A B
default volunteer
when cond A injured
when bestbond B A
text {A} needs the ultrasound probe from another ship's medical kit, and the next scheduled transfer window is days away.
option send | Send the kit | The fleet holds formation tight for an unscheduled transfer, and the kit rides the line across alone. {A}'s wrist is scanned and splinted by lunch, and the anomaly report runs to four pages.
  kit A
  res fuel -1
  morale A 6
option volunteer | {B} brings it over | {B} rides the line across with the kit in an unscheduled window and splints the wrist personally. The report calls it "nominal". Six ships read it, and every one of them knows better.
  kitfrom B A
  move B A
  res fuel -1
  bond A B 12
  morale B 4
